# =============================================================================
# Nexus QA — .gitignore
# All real product source lives under Nexus_power/. The repository ROOT is a
# scratch area accumulated from live iteration on the VM (deploy/debug/patch/
# verify scripts + docker-cp'd VM snapshots) and must NOT be committed.
# =============================================================================

# ---- Python ----
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ---- Node / client build ----
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/

# ---- Local tooling / agent + editor state ----
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/

# ---- Deploy-gate RUNTIME state (M0.4 / T-GT-04) ----
# The golden-crawl baseline is git-tracked, reviewable evidence and must stay
# byte-identical across a gate run. Per-host mutable bookkeeping — how many runs
# a never-met floor has been unmet, and which services the last deploy touched —
# lives in these files instead. Committing either would dirty the tree on every
# gate run and turn the next `git pull` on the VM into a merge conflict.
.gate_runtime_state.json
.deploy_manifest.json
.last_green_deploy

# ---- Archives, images, logs, patches (scratch artifacts) ----
*.tgz
*.tar.gz
*.log
*.patch
/*.png

# =============================================================================
# Root-level scratch scripts & docker-cp'd VM snapshots (anchored to repo root
# with a leading slash so nothing under Nexus_power/ is ever matched).
# =============================================================================
